 "review": {
  "score": 6.0,
  "round": 1,
  "problems": [
   "At a glance the shape reads as a pie dish, cake tin or wire basket rather than a giant clam. The top shell is a smooth octagon with no scalloped, wavy lip, and the gold rim follows the plain outline, so the clam silhouette is lost.",
   "The lower shell's ribs are thin dark 'graph' lines that all meet at one point (0,0) on a dark fill. In the scene they look like a wire cage or spokes, not fluted shell.",
   "The upper shell's ribs are thin steel lines on a pale fill. They read as spokes or a fan, not deep flutes. The shell looks flat and pale cream rather than brushed metal.",
   "The inside of the clam reads as flat beige/cream, not a dark purple-blue mantle. The pearl doesn't stand out against it and the opening doesn't read as a hollow.",
   "It is too wide and shallow: about 112 wide and only 82 tall, about 1.4:1. Next to the person it looks like a low tray, and the top shell barely reads as raised open. Its height against the person is fine, roughly knee to lower thigh."
  ]
 },
 "for": "a giant clam with a pearl, about knee high",
 "source": "minted",
 "created": "2026-11-02",
 "sprite": {
  "w": 126.0,
